# PRIORITY 0: DATA INTEGRITY — Implementation Plan

## Mission
Fix all data integrity issues that cause conflicting metrics, duplicate records, dashboard inconsistencies, multiple sources of truth, orphan records, and broken relationships. Establish **one authoritative source of truth** for every entity in the system.

---

## Executive Summary of Issues Found

After exhaustive audit of every file in the codebase, **7 critical data integrity violations** have been identified:

| # | Issue | Severity | Root Cause |
|---|-------|----------|------------|
| DI-1 | Dual Candidate Identity System | 🔴 Critical | `profiles` table AND `candidates` table both store candidate data with no FK relationship |
| DI-2 | Dual Application Tracking | 🔴 Critical | `job_applications` AND `candidate_applications` store the same data independently |
| DI-3 | Fabricated Financial Metrics | 🟡 High | Admin Dashboard computes fake valuations, balance sheets from headcount × hardcoded multipliers |
| DI-4 | Role Source of Truth Conflict | 🟡 High | Auth metadata, profiles table, and login "self-heal" create circular role overwrites |
| DI-5 | Inconsistent Headcount Metrics | 🟠 Medium | Admin Dashboard, HR Dashboard, and Analytics page each compute "Total Employees" differently |
| DI-6 | Analytics Computed Differently Across Pages | 🟠 Medium | Performance scores, completion rates, department counts have different formulas per page |
| DI-7 | Payroll Figures from Multiple Sources | 🟠 Medium | `payroll_ledger`, `profiles.payroll_ctc`, and hardcoded salary estimates all used in different places |

